{
  "id": "DP090",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Pilonidal cyst excision",
  "description": "Pilonidal cyst excision is surgical removal of a cyst at the base of your tailbone that becomes infected or painful. Your surgeon removes the cyst and surrounding tissue under local or general anesthesia. After removal, the wound is closed with stitches or left to heal from inside out depending on your situation. This condition often recurs if not properly treated. Some surgeons use specialized closure techniques to reduce recurrence. Recovery typically takes one to three weeks with pain management and wound care. Once healed, you can return to normal activities.",
